WHY THIS IS A SECOND FILE AND NOT AN EDIT TO `COMMIT`
-----------------------------------------------------
  Rule 1 clause 1 forbids writing to anything under third_party/, `COMMIT`
  included, and its rationale is that a local edit voids the provenance
  record. A NEW file with its own record voids nothing:
  `git status --porcelain third_party/` reports new untracked paths and no
  `M`. This is the shape third_party/cq_free_pairing/ already took, for the
  same reason (bd remember rule1-unsatisfied-for-the-ported-analysis-vendor-it,
  point 1).

  It is also forced by a SECOND fact that file records: the three artefacts
  pin at DIFFERENT revisions and one COMMIT file cannot say so. `COMMIT`
  names a6a92fe for opcode_table.yaml; the two tables below were last touched
  at two other revisions, years apart from it and from each other. Merging
  them would put three "Pinned revision (HEAD)" lines in one file — the shape
  a drift check cannot read.

  AND `COMMIT`'s "NOT vendored (deliberately)" SECTION IS NOW STALE AND MAY
  NOT BE CORRECTED THERE. It calls the scope of these two tables "an open
  scope question, not a settled fact". PRD-v2 §6.1 SETTLED it on 2026-09-17 —
  v2 vendors both — and docs/cqrt_census.txt already records that the
  correction cannot be made in `COMMIT` under Rule 1. This file is where the
  settled answer lives.

