Verification of the copy
------------------------
  `cp -f` from the paths above; sha256 of source and copy are identical, and
  BOTH MATCH THE VALUES third_party/cq_lang/COMMIT HAS RECORDED SINCE
  2026-08-14 — which is the strongest corroboration available here, because
  that file was written thirteen months of upstream history ago and has not
  been touched since. Neither table has moved in that time.

  The sha256s are independently corroborated INSIDE CQ_lang: each generated
  header carries its source table's hash in its banner —
    /Users/sorenwilkening/Desktop/Projects/CQ_lang/runtime/cq_intrinsic_templates.h:1
    /* AUTOGENERATED - do not edit. yaml-sha256: b22cf3a3...6104313e */
    /Users/sorenwilkening/Desktop/Projects/CQ_lang/runtime/cq_libm_templates.h:1
    /* AUTOGENERATED - do not edit. yaml-sha256: c3be3d43...0a630a41b */
  so these copies are provably the exact revisions that produced the shipped
  headers, and therefore the exact revisions tests/abi/'s two new manifests
  were extracted from. Declaration counts at this revision: 389 and 12.

  2,479 + 389 + 12 = 2,880, and the three symbol sets are PAIRWISE DISJOINT
  (PRD-v2 §6.1 measured it; re-measured 2026-09-19 against
